WEBVTT

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.570
<i>He's staying behind alone to play 
in the Takamatsu Memorial Cup?!</i>

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.070
<i>Taichi's getting the jump on me again!</i>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.930
Ch-Chihaya-chan...

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.710
<b>Skree!</b>

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:24.830
<i>Why?!</i>

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.640
<i>Why didn't he say anything?! 
Why'd he go alone?!</i>

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.710
<i>Why?! Why?!</i>

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.290
He...

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:43.340
He's Taichi. Of course 
he couldn't tell me.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.110
Taichi got the jump on me!

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.620
I'm here to practice.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:48.270
Practice?!

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.480
Why?!

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:55.500
Exactly. He couldn't tell you 
because it's who he is.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.460
But if you rationalize it like that,
you'll stop thinking.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.710
So keep thinking, Chihaya-chan.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.910
Think about why he does this.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.090
<i>Why...</i>

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.430
<i>Why? Why, why?</i>

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:16.380
<i>Why does Taichi always go off on his own?</i>

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:30.100
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.930
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:38.970
Verse 21

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:38.970
To restore
my faith

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.000
Mashima-sama, yes? 
We've been expecting you.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.980
<i>We'll see stormy weather across 
Japan starting tomorrow...</i>

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:47.930
<b>High</b>

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.040
<i>In the Master and Queen karuta matches
 that were held today,</i>

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.560
<i>Wakamiya Shinobu-san,
a high schooler from Kyoto,</i>

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.320
<i>successfully defended her crown as Queen 
in her third consecutive title win.</i>

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.320
<b>Still the Best Competitive Karuta Player in Japan
<u>The Queen Wins Her Third Consecutive Title!!</u></b>

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.580
<i>How should I fight?</i>

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:04.240
<i>I'm kind of looking forward to 
next year's Queen match.</i>

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.620
<i>How should I fight?</i>

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.290
<b>Karuta</b>

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.290
<b>Master retracts his retirement declaration!! Wins fifth consecutive title!!</b>

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:11.280
<i>Okay. I'll give you one
more year... for free.</i>

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:16.270
<i>I can't even think about next year.</i>

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:19.260
I'll come here to beat you!

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:23.810
<i>Dr. Harada is </i>my<i> mentor.</i>

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.730
<i>I should have been the one to say that.</i>

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:56.150
<i>I don't think I could face Arata
and keep a cool head.</i>

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:58.920
<i>How should I fight?</i>

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:00.950
<i>Against Arata...</i>

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.170
<i>Against myself?</i>

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.930
January 11th

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.930
Otsuka Karuta Memorial Hall, Tokyo

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.940
New Year's Karuta Tournament
 (Classes A, B, C)

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.940
Class D Tournament Held at Bunkyo Sports Center

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.350
Dang, Mashima's entered in this one, too.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:20.170
It was so he could play in either?
He really had all the bases covered.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.740
<b>Rich, too...</b>

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:22.750
He's a lot more serious
about karuta than I realized.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.740
<b>Both have
entry fees</b>

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:28.380
Kana-chan's serious, too!
A kimono so early in the new year!

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.250
So serious!

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.990
It's <i>because</i> it's so early in the new year!

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.500
<b>And here's another one who's serious...</b>

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:42.250
In my mind,

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.580
"last year" ended with the 
Master and Queen matches,

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:49.070
and "this year" starts with 
the New Year's Tournament.

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:50.690
Oh, I get that!

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:51.520
Me, too!

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.770
<b>Ayase Chihaya</b>

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.120
We'll be in our third year of high school soon.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.760
Our last year.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.020
Everything is too precious to waste.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.180
Every match, every moment,

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:05.060
is too precious not to take seriously.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.510
Oe-senpai's right!

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:12.910
<b>Here for support</b>

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.090
Why are you in a kimono, too?!

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:12.620
Not that you're any match for me,
since you're in Class D.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:12.910
Huh?!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:17.490
To secure my position as the next 
president of the Mizusawa Karuta Club,

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:20.720
I'm going to win today 
and advance to Class B!

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.550
<b>You can do it, bro!!</b>

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.550
Here for 
support

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:21.540
The next president?!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.200
<i>The next president...</i>

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:29.820
<i>That's right. Our club won't 
stay the same forever.</i>

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.960
<i>It's going to change.</i>

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:36.030
<i>We'll all go our separate ways, just like today...</i>

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:41.940
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:44.430
<i>Why, Taichi?</i>

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.520
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.630
<i>Taichi is...</i>

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.300
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.570
<i>...fighting his own battles.</i>

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.280
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.070
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.450
<i>I'll have to go into this without answers.</i>

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:03.940
Class A competitors will now be 
matched up. Gather, please.

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:07.000
<i>I'll fight my own battles.</i>

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.830
Class B competitors,

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.990
please take your assigned seats.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.850
<b>This is the year! 
Class A</b>

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.990
<i>I'll fight my own battles!</i>

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:12.590
Retro-kun?!

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:13.840
I haven't seen you in ages!

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:18.850
<b>Same Day 
Shiga Prefecture 
Omi Jingu</b>

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:18.850
Takamatsu Memorial Cup 
at the Learning Center

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.200
That's him! The one we saw on Nico!

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.030
Oh!

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:24.540
I saw that! What he said 
was pretty crazy, huh?

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:27.900
You know who he is, right?
The grandson of Eternal Master Wataya!

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.150
Oh, Wataya-kun, Wataya-kun!

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.900
Mr. Yoshioka.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.210
You really surprised me yesterday.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:37.170
I've never seen you so proactive.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:43.930
You can't afford to lose 
any tournaments now, huh?

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:48.420
<b>Bluuuuush</b>

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:48.420
Right... Right...

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.870
I know you're a strong player,

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.680
and I believe you have room to grow, too.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.810
As long as you maintain the fortitude 
to win one match at a time,

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.090
you'll make it.

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:00.800
Go get 'em.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.240
Oh...

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.300
If there's anything I hope for,

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:09.490
it's that you have someone 
like Sato Kiyohiko, grade 9.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.060
Huh?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.080
I'm the only one who stayed.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:31.070
I'm looking forward to today.

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:35.850
<i>There's a reason why I...</i>

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:37.640
<i>...can't...</i>

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:39.760
<i>...lose!</i>

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:47.100
<i>To become, in my vast popularity,
the (obvious choice for the) next club president!</i>

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:52.240
Retro can probably do it

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:52.240
<b>Probably</b>

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:52.240
<b>This is the year! 
Class A</b>

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.560
<i>But I'm still Class B.</i>

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.230
<i>I have the skill, but bad luck
has thwarted my rise to Class A!</i>

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:54.620
Oh, I got that one, right?

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.990
Huh? Er, but...

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:59.100
No, I think I touched it 
faster from this angle.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:00.150
Huh? Which one?

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:02.470
Oh, we're starting there?

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:04.990
You couldn't tell? Oh, okay.

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:07.070
Never mind, then.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:09.130
<b>Confused...</b>

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:09.130
<b>This is the year! 
Class A</b>

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:11.820
Uh...

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.270
Huh? What?

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:16.960
Oh, uh... just... hmm...

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:19.430
Yeah, never mind.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:22.350
We can sort all that out later.
Let's just keep going.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.300
<i>The Tamaru siblings are 
as annoying as ever.</i>

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.790
<i>They'd be good enough if 
they just played normally.</i>

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:29.690
<i>Isn't that what makes them so strong?</i>

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.310
<i>It ticks you off and throws you off-pace.</i>

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:34.570
<i>He's an unusual type...</i>

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:36.080
Oh, sorry.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.690
Does the way I move my cards 
make it hard to play?

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.980
Sorry. I get that a lot.

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:45.790
No, it's fine.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:51.340
<i>What? She's such a frail girl, and yet...</i>

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:55.060
<i>her core is sturdier than mine?</i>

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.330
<i>After I determined... {poem 63}</i>

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.690
<i>And light!</i>

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.690
<i>The sight of Shinobu-chan crumbling to pieces,</i>

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.170
<i>and when she recovered...</i>

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:08.690
<i>Dr. Harada's passion,</i>

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.230
<i>and Suo-san's strength...</i>

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:14.090
<i>Arata's determination,</i>

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:16.900
<i>and Taichi's challenge...</i>

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.920
<i>By clashing together, they change.</i>

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:25.770
<i>Can I make my own beginning, too?</i>

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:30.320
<i>I forgot my tasuki again!</i>

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.540
<i>Ms. Miyauchi's tasuki!</i>

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:39.960
<i>A new year, a new day...</i>

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:52.510
<i>Mashima-senpai's the only 
one who's not here.</i>

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:57.330
<i>I wonder why... A new year has begun...</i>

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:02.840
<i>But it's the end that I'm more concerned about.</i>

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.620
<b>Omi Learning Center</b>

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.240
Master Suo!

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:12.530
Excuse me. I was hoping I could
have my trophy sent home.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:15.060
Oh... Head to the staff room.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:17.340
The Takamatsu Memorial Cup's
going on right now,

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.500
so be quiet, okay?

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:22.500
Man, the Nagumo Society's tough! That's just nasty!

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:25.140
Four of them have made it to the quarters.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:27.110
We're drawing the fourth round match-ups.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.230
Murao Shinichi 

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:41.530
Okay. I'll give you one 
more year... for free.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:44.450
<i>A one-year extension.</i>

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.710
Mashima Taichi

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.540
Wataya Arata

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:52.110
<i>In one year,</i>

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:55.540
<i>364 days later...</i>

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:06.570
<i>who's going to have the last laugh?</i>

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:12.060
Mashima Taichi

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:16.530
<b>Nagumo Society</b>

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:20.420
The Nagumo Society's black T-shirts

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:26.080
<b>Hehehehehe {rainbow, repeats}</b>

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:22.770
look pretty intimidating 
in a scenario like this.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:26.080
Is everyone except the black-shirts 
gonna end up eliminated?

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:38.930
<i>I can't look him in the eye.</i>

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:39.710
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.460
<i>I know I need to keep a cool head, but I'm...</i>

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:45.670
<i>Arata's looking at me.</i>

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.330
<i>He's acting normal.</i>

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:48.220
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.760
Arata, you had an even number, right?

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:54.280
You should be on the side nearest the wall.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:54.760
Huh?

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:58.010
Oh... Sorry. I got mixed up.

00:11:58.010 --> 00:11:58.850
Same.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:10.890
Please place your cards.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:17.870
<i>The Master!</i>

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.140
<i>What's he doing here?</i>

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.790
<i>I've seen this before...</i>

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:29.720
<i>Wataya Arata's Preferred Layout</i>

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.190
Arata's card layout?

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:31.650
I'm supposed to be a virtual Arata?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:41.640
One's trying to be Suo Hisashi,
and one's trying to be Wataya Arata.

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:54.780
<i>Are those two... friends?</i>

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:02.690
Let's play karuta!

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:09.510
No, that was mine!

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:10.430
I took that one!

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:12.010
No way! I swept that one!

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:15.630
<i>That's unusual. Arata-kun is arguing.</i>

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.150
I swept it, too!

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:19.210
Well, I touched it first!

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:19.640
Anyway,

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:23.390
even if we hit it at the 
same time, I get the card!

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:27.060
<i>Oh?</i>

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:30.500
<i>He moved for his opponent's 
lower right side,</i>

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:32.820
<i>then changed course to the opponent's left.</i>

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:37.030
<i>Then he got him to agree that 
they hit it at the same time.</i>

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:40.080
<i>Yeah, anyone would find him 
annoying to play against.</i>

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:44.500
<i>He's definitely a Shiranami Society member.</i>

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:48.050
<i>That's definitely Dr. Harada's offensive karuta.</i>

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:52.050
<i>I can't let him take even one card easily.</i>

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:55.290
<i>I have to play dirty karuta against Arata.</i>

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:59.330
<i>Pressure him to fight hard against
 someone he sees as beneath him...</i>

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:10.100
<i>Long last we meet...</i>

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.110
<i>Oh, nice one.</i>

00:14:20.260 --> 00:14:22.260
...like flowing water.

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:25.490
<i>He was like this when he played 
the Queen in the summer, too.</i>

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:26.850
<i>That face...</i>

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:30.640
<i>That aura...</i>

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:34.970
<i>Right... Take them like that, move like this.</i>

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:36.410
<i>I can visualize it.</i>

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:39.810
<i>Send "As this," cross over between 
"Would the" and "Would this"...</i>

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:41.740
<i>More...</i>

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.030
<i>Maybe I...</i>

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:48.150
<i>always looked down on Taichi in karuta.</i>

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:54.270
<i>I thought it'd be difficult 
to play against Taichi.</i>

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:59.950
<i>But it's like I can feel 
my heart growing bigger.</i>

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:03.530
<i>I'm that happy!</i>

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:05.580
<i>Atta boy!</i>

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:13.210
<i>Would the mountain cherry blossoms...</i>

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.530
<i>His opponent used a cross 
against him, too?!</i>

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.670
<i>Wait, no.</i>

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:22.530
<i>He was covering "Would this" to block him,</i>

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.600
<i>which killed the speed 
of Arata-kun's swing.</i>

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.760
<i>He then went on to swipe "Would the" away.</i>

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.850
<i>He set out to defeat his cross.</i>

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.180
Arata, did you...

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.710
say something to Chihaya back in the fall?

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:49.700
Uh... Yeah. I did.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:56.560
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:01.030
I see.

00:16:03.010 --> 00:16:04.950
I play offensive karuta

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.600
The more I want a card, 
the faster I let it go.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.840
Then I go in determined to take it.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:29.400
Oh, shoot! I was just testing 
my luck! Is this okay?!

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:31.550
Class B Winner

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:31.550
<b>I didn't mean to do that</b>

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.540
Is it okay for me to win?!

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:35.110
The Tamaru sister won in Class B? For real?

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:37.160
She's gonna be even more insufferable now.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.170
Those other guys need to get it together!

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:52.340
"In order to... "

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:53.080
Huh?

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:58.480
"In order to restore my 
faith in this world... "

00:16:58.480 --> 00:16:59.380
Huh?

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:10.380
<i>Emperor Gotoba 
In order to restore my faith in this world,
 I have learned to both love and hate my fellow man</i>

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:03.490
The last card that was taken from me today.

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:06.300
It's exactly how I feel right now...

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:09.880
What a miserable poem for
Emperor Gotoba to leave behind...

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.740
You've gotta keep this a secret,

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:15.510
but all of the "In" cards 
are my worst ones.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:19.330
Not only the ones that start with "In," but 
the ones with "in" in the second verse, too!

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:22.400
They always confuse me for a second, 
and there are so many of them...

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.880
<i>I've been doing this for 
ten years, and still...</i>

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.170
I'm not cut out to play karuta!

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:33.820
Class A Finals

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:37.520
I wanted to be a club president

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:42.170
who had talent and could be trusted,
just like Sudo-san...

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:55.910
Retro-kun, did you know?

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:56.810
Huh?

00:17:57.240 --> 00:18:00.590
Emperor Gotoba's poem is number 99,

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:04.140
and his son, Emperor Juntoku, 
wrote number 100.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:26.580
<i>Emperor Juntoku 
Would this old palace courtyard and the eaves strewn 
with weeds be as dear now, those were the good old days</i>

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:07.720
It's the last poem in the Hundred Poets,

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:12.660
and it's packed with deep, genuine feelings 
about the end of noble society.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:18.040
<i>Weeping ferns grow on the roof of the 
once-prosperous imperial palace.</i>

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:23.720
<i>Memories of the good old days, too dear and 
numerous to recollect, are yet brought to mind.</i>

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:25.200
Do you understand?

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:31.670
It's nothing like your petty frustration 
over being stuck in Class B!

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:33.090
<b>Shock</b>

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:34.720
Hey, Retro.

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:35.980
Retro-senpai.

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:37.500
What're you doing?

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:40.430
Sudo-senpai's gonna kill you if
you're not in there to root for him.

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:42.730
He said he's gonna treat us all later.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:46.270
If he wins, it'll be yakiniku,
and if he loses, it's beef bowls.

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:50.060
I'm sorry, guys... I lost...

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:52.740
I'm the next club president, 
and I'm still in Class B...

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:53.580
Huh?

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:55.690
That doesn't matter.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.360
I mean, you in Class A?

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:58.730
We never expected that.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.740
<b>Shock</b>

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.250
Let's go!

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:03.680
Think we'll get yakiniku?

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:05.250
Maybe beef bowls...

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:07.630
Meat... If I eat some meat...

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:12.130
<i>Maybe what I said was mean,
but I won't let go of his hand.</i>

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:15.360
Up we go!

00:19:16.390 --> 00:19:18.900
What should I make next time?

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:21.830
Actually, what prefecture will 
the next tournament be in?

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:24.120
It's like I'm on tour!

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:36.300
<i>When was the last time I played Ayase?</i>

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:37.780
<i>Quite a while?</i>

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:44.030
<i>Was it then? Tch, what a lousy memory.</i>

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:50.120
<i>Back then, she was relying on game sense
and only cared about taking cards quickly.</i>

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:52.970
<i>But now, she's grown in a lot of ways.</i>

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:55.490
<i>She's grown, and yet...</i>

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.930
<b>Ahhh!</b>

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:05.700
<i>Crap! Damn it!</i>

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:08.620
Thank you very much.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.310
Th-Th...

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.360
Thank you very much.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.230
I had a feeling about it before...

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:21.160
But you really can make yourself totally empty.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:25.320
Even when you keep
absorbing stuff from around you...

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.590
How do you do it?

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:32.430
I guess sounds resonate 
better in emptiness.

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:41.470
<b>Zzzz</b>

00:20:40.730 --> 00:20:41.470
Hey!

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:03.870
Want one?

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:19.590
January 11th 
Bunkyo 
New Year's 
Karuta Tournament

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:19.590
Winner 
Ayase Chihaya

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:23.090
Omi Jingu Takamatsu
 Memorial Cup 
Runner-Up 
Wataya Arata

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:23.090
Winner 
Murao Shinichi

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:30.100
4th Prize (Quarterfinalist)

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:30.100
Mashima Taichi
